A||||2||GarethWright||A/C Compressor or Clutch?||||1||
Z||000000||GarethWright||04-03-2001||01:43 AM||||Hello,<BR>When I turn on the AC on my 87 gt, I get a Really nasty squealing sound, which I know is the belt.  When I tightened the belt, the AC worked great for about 2 days, then it started squealing again, and didn't cool the air at all.  I looked at the belt, really loose again, this was a Brand new belt, and the compressor hadn't moved on its adjustments at all.  <BR>Is this likely to be caused by the Clutch seizing up, or is the whole Compressor shot?<BR>Thanks<BR>Gareth<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||04-03-2001||09:24 AM||||I'd say the whole compressor.  If the clutch locked, it would just run the A/C whether it was on or off.  Sounds like the oil and freon leaked out of your compressor and it's burned up.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||04-03-2001||10:47 AM||||If you reach down to the front of the compressor. (Engine shut off of course) If you can turn the compressor (center of pulley and not the pulley ifself then the compressor is probably alright. If the center does not turn the compressor is shot.||||reg||1
